{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.A_dependence_forces_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.A_dependence_forces_complete","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityTopologySelection.lean#L69-L78","doc":"**Topology selection (the #2507 thesis).** A Pauli-restricted binding\nwhose p-n bond count differs between two `(Z,N)`-nuclei (i.e. is genuinely\n`A`-dependent) cannot be realized on the chain topology: the chain forces\nequality. Contrapositive of `chain_binding_A_independent`; the only\nremaining parameter-free topology that supports the differing count is the\ncomplete graph (`complete_pn_strictMono_N`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.complete_pn_strictMono_N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.complete_pn_strictMono_N","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityTopologySelection.lean#L59-L67","doc":"**Structural result 2 (complete ⇒ A-dependent).** On the complete graph\nthe p-n bond count strictly increases with the neutron number whenever a\nproton is present, so the binding is genuinely `A`-dependent. (Symmetric in\n`Z` by `Nat.mul_comm`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.complete_pn_eq_ZN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.complete_pn_eq_ZN","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityTopologySelection.lean#L56-L57","doc":"The complete-graph p-n bond count equals `Z · N` definitionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.chain_binding_A_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.chain_binding_A_independent","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityTopologySelection.lean#L46-L54","doc":"**Structural result 1 (chain ⇒ A-independent).** Under the Pauli\nrestriction (only p-n pairs bind) the chain p-n bond count is the *same*\n(`= 1`) for every nucleus with at least one proton and one neutron, so the\nbinding carries no `A`-dependence — the constant-binding collapse observed\nas the 3.89 MeV flat line in the #2507 table. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.completePnBonds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.completePnBonds","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityTopologySelection.lean#L41-L44","doc":"p-n bond count on the **complete-graph** topology: every proton pairs\nwith every neutron, `Z · N` bonds. Matches `_counts(... \"complete\")[\"pn\"]\n= Z * N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.chainPnBonds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityTopologySelection.chainPnBonds","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityTopologySelection.lean#L36-L39","doc":"p-n bond count on the **linear-chain** topology: a single proton–neutron\ninterface bond when both species are present, independent of `A = Z + N`.\nMatches `_counts(... \"chain\")[\"pn\"] = 1` in the #2507 probe. ","signatureChunk":0}]}